cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "InsightTrack: a self-hosted web analytics platform with a dual-database architecture"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ray
    given-names: Nishikanta
    # Add `orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"` here before archiving
    # to Zenodo or submitting to JOSS — both expect a persistent author ID.
repository-code: "https://github.com/NishikantaRay/InsightTrack"
abstract: >-
  InsightTrack is a self-hosted web analytics platform that separates its write
  path from its read path across two databases. PostgreSQL is the system of
  record for tracking events, authentication and site management; an embedded
  DuckDB instance, kept current by an incremental sync process, serves every
  analytics query. The split lets the transactional store stay normalised and
  write-optimised while analytical aggregations run against a columnar engine in
  the same process, with no separate warehouse to operate. The platform includes
  an allowlist-validated SQL editor scoped to a single tenant, configurable
  retention that deletes from both stores, and honours Do Not Track and Global
  Privacy Control signals.
keywords:
  - web analytics
  - self-hosted
  - DuckDB
  - PostgreSQL
  - OLAP
  - privacy
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-28"
